                        "entry_id": "30753e0c-5b5a-3a78-9b5b-b9180f311fe9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To brainstorm ideas."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72571081-09be-4344-8a8f-29e73890a54b",
                                "sense_id": "85fb3806-1cae-30b0-825f-2cf4251d959a",
                                "text": "Maybe, and I'm just spitballing here, maybe, we have a responsibility as officers to train Santiago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5c5fa87-fcd5-429d-a850-f4ce3e7ad5a4",
                                "sense_id": "85fb3806-1cae-30b0-825f-2cf4251d959a",
                                "text": "—Yes, Wheeler?\n—Question. Maybe a stupid one, but I'm just spitballing here."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a4e332b-de2a-47fa-b5f9-3760f96749e9",
                                "sense_id": "85fb3806-1cae-30b0-825f-2cf4251d959a",
                                "text": "What happens, though, if you, the filmmaker, can't get the malevolence to work? That's where Jaws had its happy misfortune, its felix culpa. When the mechanical sharks failed to work[…][Steven] Spielberg and his cast had nothing to do but hole up evening after evening in a Martha's Vineyard house and spitball about the script, story and characters."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
